{"duration": 54.263, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "A naval officer hoisted a massive lantern atop a rusted pole.", "start": 0.08, "end": 3.791}, {"beat": 0, "text": "He balanced the weight, sweat dripping, while the sea roared.", "start": 4.011, "end": 6.747}, {"beat": 1, "text": "His crew laughed, saying a tower would never change the storm.", "start": 7.167, "end": 10.142}, {"beat": 1, "text": "They muttered that a wooden pier could do the job.", "start": 10.362, "end": 12.73}, {"beat": 2, "text": "The government orders the tower\u2019s steel skeleton to rise in 1910.", "start": 13.15, "end": 17.026}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Engineers sketch blueprints on cramped desks.", "start": 17.245, "end": 19.51}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Workers weld the frame while ships wait for safe passage.", "start": 19.73, "end": 22.72}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Every night the unfinished tower glints in fog.", "start": 22.94, "end": 25.213}, {"beat": 3, "text": "You see, it\u2019s like putting a bright sign on a dark road you travel every day.", "start": 25.633, "end": 29.271}, {"beat": 4, "text": "The real reason: the state needed a high\u2011point to record weather.", "start": 29.691, "end": 32.973}, {"beat": 4, "text": "The lighthouse would measure wind, rain, and tides for the port.", "start": 33.193, "end": 36.3}, {"beat": 4, "text": "At the same time it broadcast a glowing symbol of modern Japan.", "start": 36.52, "end": 40.09}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Foreign visitors would see the flash and think Japan was advanced.", "start": 40.31, "end": 43.536}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Ironically, the lighthouse\u2019s flash later guided not only ships, but also the nation\u2019s own propaganda ships.", "start": 43.956, "end": 50.232}, {"beat": 5, "text": "The tower became a beacon for both safety and pride.", "start": 50.452, "end": 53.143}], "words": [{"w": "A", "start": 0.124, "end": 0.174, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "naval", "start": 0.224, "end": 0.524, "line": 0, "beat"